WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:01.450
Okay.

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:02.450
Hillary Clinton.

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.560
We've heard from Hillary Clinton.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:10.759
Hillary Clinton says that Joe Biden should
not concede the election to Donald Trump in

00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:13.559
the immediate aftermath of November 3rd.

00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:15.719
Under any circumstances.

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:21.360
Until and if it becomes clear that Joe Biden
has actually lost the election.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.090
There's an interesting new interview.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:27.490
Clinton was interviewed by Jennifer Palmieri
for the Showtime program.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:33.660
The circus and right wingers are losing their
minds about what Hillary said.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.410
Sean Hannity is feverish.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.809
Lee tweeting about it.

00:00:36.809 --> 00:00:38.589
People are going crazy.

00:00:38.589 --> 00:00:40.170
It's really not a big deal, actually.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:43.120
What Hillary Clinton says makes a lot of sense.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.559
And in fact, it shouldn't even be super controversial.

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:47.839
Let's take a look at it, then we'll discuss.

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:52.710
So we've got to have a massive legal operation.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.929
I know the Biden campaign is working on that.

00:00:55.929 --> 00:00:57.600
We have to have poll workers.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:04.470
And I urge people who are able to be a poll
worker.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:12.580
We have to have our own teams of people to
counter the force of intimidation that the

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:16.310
Republicans and Trump are going to put outside
polling places.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:22.220
This is a big organizational challenge, but
at least we know more about what they're going

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.220
to do.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:29.730
And, you know, Joe Biden should not concede
under any circumstances because I think this

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:35.030
is going to drag out and eventually I do believe
he will win.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:42.670
If we don't give an inch and if we are as
focused and relentless as the other side is.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:44.550
So this is actually good advice.

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:47.910
And Democrats Democrats sometimes are pushovers.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:49.390
Let's be completely frank.

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:52.950
And there really is no incentive to concede
early period.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:58.810
Now, people like Sean Hannity and others are
pretending that what Hillary Clinton is saying

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:03.850
is never concede, no matter what, even if
you lose the popular vote and the electoral

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:09.430
vote handily and there's no foul play that
appears to have taken place and there's no

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:10.430
right.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.520
That's not what Hillary Clinton is saying.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:19.290
Hillary Clinton is astutely pointing out Trump
is not going to concede if it's close.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.380
Trump is going to claim that it's rigged.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:25.190
Donald Trump is trying to rig it and planning
to rig it.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:30.370
So why should Joe Biden concede if there's
any possibility that he actually won?

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:35.380
Now, this could be because of mail in ballots
that had have maybe will not yet be counted

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.209
as of November 3rd at midnight.

00:02:37.209 --> 00:02:38.950
That's one possibility.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.140
It could be because of other types of voter
suppression.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.740
It could be for any number of different reasons.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:50.930
And I was actually thinking back to the year
2000, which 2000 was sort of the first presidential

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.510
election I paid close attention to.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:55.960
I remember I was in high school and there
were you know, you started to figure out who

00:02:55.960 --> 00:03:02.210
are the few right wing kids in my very liberal
high school and who's following politics and

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:03.210
who's not.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.220
And I remember paying close attention to that
election.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.959
It was Bush v. Gore and it came down to Florida.

00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:11.730
As many of you may remember, Al Gore won the
popular vote.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.620
Nationally ultimately lost Florida.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:19.640
And when people think back to that, I was
recently talking to people who misremember

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.510
the crux of what happened in the year 2000
in Florida.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:28.239
A lot of people correctly remember that there
was a recount started in Florida and that

00:03:28.239 --> 00:03:33.830
then Republican secretary of state in Florida,
Katherine Harris, got involved.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:40.550
Ultimately, the Supreme Court stopped the
recount and the state went to George W. Bush

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:43.110
by about 500 votes.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:48.880
And when people think back now, they often
think if the Supreme Court hadn't stopped

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:53.459
the recount, Al Gore would have won, would
have won Florida and thus would have won the

00:03:53.459 --> 00:03:54.840
presidency.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:04:00.760
That's not likely the case because there was
a secondary controversy in Florida in the

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.060
year 2000.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:07.790
The details of which people still argue about,
but it was about votes sent in by mail, many

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:13.770
from overseas, a bunch of different scenarios,
a bunch of different ballots which were misplaced

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.359
and thrown out and just disappeared.

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:22.900
OK, so the exact details are less relevant
than the realization that in all likelihood,

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:27.770
the recount that was stopped, George W. Bush
was probably going to win that recount if

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:29.280
it had been completed.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:35.710
The real problem was the problem of the ballots
that were not going to be part of the equation

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.530
that were that were gone.

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:42.470
And likewise, in this upcoming election, there
are likely to be a ton of different layers

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:50.280
in the subterfuge, including in absentee ballots,
voter suppression, voter purges, meddling

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.190
of different kinds.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:57.700
Trump trying to use the judges that he so
famously has appointed to his advantage on

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:58.830
and on and on.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:05.090
And so what Hillary Clinton is suggesting
is not that if Joe Biden loses fair and square,

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:06.660
he never concede.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:11.160
What Hillary Clinton is suggesting is that
until it is really, truly, all completely

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:17.200
said and done and it is completely clear that
Joe Biden has lost, there is no reason for

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.940
Joe Biden to concede now.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:23.120
I think we also have to remember because people
are going crazy pulling their hair out about

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.010
over this, as if Hillary Clinton, Hillary
Clinton is saying something crazy.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.070
Remember that conceding is merely a formality.

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:30.570
Doesn't matter.

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:36.710
Whether the the losing candidate concedes
has no bearing on what happens on January

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:37.830
20th.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:44.340
And when it might come down to lawsuits and
courts and the opinions of judges, maybe judges

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:46.640
selected by Donald Trump.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:48.310
You don't want to do anything.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:53.470
The optics of which might make it easier for
a judge to hand anything to Donald Trump.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:59.440
And although conceding is merely a formality,
much like running up the score in the popular

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:06.169
vote, these are optics which might provide
cover for a judge to rule in favor of Donald

00:06:06.169 --> 00:06:07.169
Trump.

00:06:07.169 --> 00:06:11.260
If it comes down to a court and likewise,
this is why I've said we have to run up the

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:15.710
popular vote, you know, in heavily blue states
like California and Massachusetts, there may

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.520
be leftists who say not going to vote.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:22.510
They don't need my vote or vote third party
because Biden's clearly going to win California.

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:24.280
He's clearly going to win Massachusetts.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.030
I disagree.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:32.700
We have to run up the score, make it harder
for a court to help Donald Trump in any way,

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:38.410
because Donald Trump is going to use every
tactic possible to steal this election.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:43.690
Joe Biden and the Democrats need to have a
specific plan for exactly how to deal with

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:45.509
every aspect of this ahead of time.

00:06:45.509 --> 00:06:47.720
I'm not sure that they do.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:52.419
Now, let's let's deal just for a moment with
what the right wingers are saying.

00:06:52.419 --> 00:06:57.260
Again, people like Hannity and some right
wingers are reacting as if Hillary Clinton

00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:01.770
is saying, even if you really lose, don't
concede.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:03.570
That's not what she's saying.

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:09.110
She's saying she believes Joe Biden is going
to win, but that there will be pressure on

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:17.070
him to concede and foul play such that he
might end up conceding before he's satisfied

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:20.380
that he really lost and that he shouldn't
do that.

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:24.500
I'm the first to tell you Biden may actually
lose.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:29.220
At least 60 million people are going to be
voting for the reelection of Donald Trump.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:31.960
Maybe 65 million, maybe 66.

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:33.250
We don't know.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:37.140
But roughly 60 something million people will
be voting for Trump's reelection.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:39.600
It's certainly plausible that Trump wins.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:45.620
And if that's the case, it's not for Joe Biden
to just insist that he really won.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:48.350
Biden will have to concede, and I'm sure he
will.

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:52.919
And it'll be up to us to deal with the reality
that we have more than 60 million people in

00:07:52.919 --> 00:07:57.720
this country who observed the last four years
and said, give me another four.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:07:58.960
That's a problem we'll have to deal with.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.600
And it's a serious problem.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:05.490
But the advice is correct to Joe Biden until
you're actually satisfied that you really

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:06.750
lost.

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:07.750
Don't concede.

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:08.860
And I hope he follows it.

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:10.760
Hopefully it won't even be close.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.419
But there's a real possibility that it will
be.

00:08:13.419 --> 00:08:17.210
And those close scenarios, as I'm going to
talk about Friday, are the ones that are going

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:19.550
to be the most difficult legally.

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:24.170
And also the most likely to lead to violence
in the streets, which I don't want to happen,

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:28.190
but I fear is a real possibility if it's close
and Trump says that it's rigged.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:30.550
I'll deal with that on Friday.

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:37.020
And what is happening in the intervening time
now is everybody's got to figure out how are

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:38.490
you planning to vote?

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:39.890
Are you voting absentee?

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:42.470
If so, are you mailing your ballot or dropping
it off?

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:43.880
Are you voting in person?

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:44.880
What's the plan?

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.310
Is it going to feel safe?

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.490
How many masks will you be wearing?

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:49.560
So on and so forth.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.910
That's what we can do in the intervening time.

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:56.950
We will have more on this, much more on our
Instagram page.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:59.450
Make sure you're following us there at David
Pakman show.

